2. Net Calibrator
The AquaStream360 Network Calibration Tool provides a specialized, sandboxed environment for safely testing, calibrating, and optimizing water distribution networks. It enables engineers to experiment with changes to pipes, pumps, junctions, and other network components without risking the integrity of the original master model.
Core Purpose
The tool functions as a controlled laboratory for water networks. Its primary objective is to support data-driven decision-making by allowing users to evaluate multiple "what-if" scenarios, identify optimal parameter values, and understand system sensitivities before implementing any permanent modifications. It bridges the gap between theoretical analysis and practical, real-world application.
Structured Three-Phase Workflow
1.	Define & Configure
Users select the elements to test (e.g., pipes, pumps, junctions), choose specific elements or the entire category, and define the attributes to modify (e.g., diameter, roughness). Test conditions can be set as ranges (e.g., 100 mm to 300 mm) or target-based (e.g., nearest to a pressure of 25 m).
2.	Simulate & Analyze
With a single action, the tool generates and executes multiple simulation scenarios. Results are explored through a range of analytical views:
o	Quick Analysis: Focused queries, such as identifying junctions where pressure falls below a set threshold in a specific scenario.
o	Detailed Automated Analysis: Comprehensive reports, frequency distributions, and time-series comparisons based on the test scope.
o	Visual Analysis: Charts and graphs highlighting trends and patterns across all scenarios.
o	Attribute Network Viewer: Maps scenario results directly onto the network. Hovering over elements provides side-by-side comparisons of all outcomes, offering a clear visualization of parameter impacts across the system.
3.	Apply & Decide
Once the optimal scenario is identified, changes can be applied intentionally. All experimentation occurs on a temporary copy; the user must explicitly choose to update the original network, ensuring that permanent changes are deliberate and verified.
Key Features and Advantages
•	Risk-Free Sandbox: Experiments never alter the original network, allowing safe exploration.
•	Intelligent Automation: Context-aware guidance, suggested default values, and automatically generated test ranges streamline scenario setup.
•	Comparative Spatial Analysis: The Attribute Network Viewer transforms tabular results into a map-based comparison, facilitating rapid identification of how parameter changes affect pressures, flows, and network performance.
•	Calibration-Ready: Supports model calibration by comparing simulated results against field-measured data, systematically identifying optimal parameter settings to enhance accuracy.
Practical Applications
•	Model Calibration: Adjust pipe roughness, demand multipliers, and other parameters to match observed sensor data.
•	Design Optimization: Evaluate different pipe diameters or pump configurations to achieve performance standards efficiently.
•	Sensitivity Analysis: Determine which parameters most influence network behavior, such as tank levels affecting downstream pressures.
•	Emergency Planning: Simulate pipe failures, fire flows, and other contingencies to assess system vulnerability and resilience.

